WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.275
The quiet hazard is fog.

2
00:00:02.525 --> 00:00:07.275
It forms when air cools to its dew point, and there are two kinds to know.

3
00:00:07.525 --> 00:00:12.275
Advection fog forms when warm, moist air moves over cooler water.

4
00:00:12.525 --> 00:00:16.750
It can last for hours, or for days, and wind doesn’t clear it.

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.600
Radiation fog forms on clear, calm nights, as the land cools.

6
00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:27.125
It drifts out over rivers, bays and harbors, and the morning sun burns it off.

7
00:00:27.375 --> 00:00:34.525
Florida’s sea fog is mostly a winter and spring problem, when warm air slides over cooler nearshore water.

8
00:00:34.775 --> 00:00:36.725
So which kind is that?

9
00:00:37.725 --> 00:00:39.600
Advection fog.

10
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.625
When visibility drops, you know the rule.

11
00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:45.550
Rule nineteen, and fog signals.

12
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:52.325
Slow to a safe speed, lights on, plot your radar targets, and post an extra lookout to listen.
